Each column is a subject and each row a requested time, giving the estimated probability of
surviving past that time.

To compare predicted curves visually, `plot_predicted_survival()` draws one step-function curve per
subject. This is especially useful for parametric models, where the smooth survival function can be
evaluated at many time points.

::: {#a44dff9b .cell execution_count=16}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Visualize predicted survival for the two new subjects
gw.plot_predicted_survival(aft, newdata=newdata)
```

