### Predicting survival

`predict()` supports the linear predictor (`type="lp"`) and survival probabilities
(`type="survival"`). Since there is no fitted distribution to evaluate, survival predictions reuse
the empirical Kaplan-Meier curve of the fitted residuals, shifted by each subject's linear
predictor, rather than a smooth closed-form curve.

::: {#153236c2 .cell execution_count=45}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Predicted survival at 6 months, 1 year, and 2 years
bj.predict(newdata, type="survival", times=[180, 365, 730], format="polars")
```

