The `n_iter` column shows how many EM iterations were needed for convergence. If `n_iter` equals
the maximum (`emmax`, default 50), the algorithm may not have converged and you should increase
`emmax`.

::: {.callout-tip}
## When to consider a cure model

A cure model is appropriate when the Kaplan-Meier curve for your data levels off well above zero,
suggesting that a fraction of subjects will never experience the event. If the KM curve continues
to decline throughout follow-up, a standard Cox or AFT model is more appropriate.
:::

## Next steps

You can now fit, compare, predict from, and diagnose parametric survival models.

- [Cox model diagnostics](cox-diagnostics.qmd) covers residuals and influence diagnostics for
the semiparametric alternative, with the same conceptual framework.
- [Cox regression](cox-regression.qmd) is the semiparametric alternative, useful when you
prefer not to assume a distribution.
- [Prediction performance](prediction-performance.qmd) evaluates any fitted model,
parametric or not.
- [Competing risks](competing-risks.qmd) handles the case of more than one type of event.
